MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_001: Wait, Lilian! You and I must talk.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_002: Ugh, this again. Let me guess, you've got a lecture\nabout propriety for me?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_003: Exactly. Don't think I haven't noticed your disrespect\nfor Her Majesty!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_004: You should educate yourself on proper speech and\ncourtly manners.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_005: I've told you it's not about that.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_006: Besides, I know all about that stuff. Or at least I did\nwhen I was little.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_007: What? Are you telling me you've been educated in\nthe ways of nobility?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_008: Don't believe me? Watch this. I mean... Ahem!\nBear witness, my good Lysander!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_009: Is she about to... She is! That's a traditional\nballroom dance!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_010: Well, well. Your footwork was immaculate. Those\nbad manners had me believing you were born poor.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_011: Um, rude. My house is actually a big deal. We've\nfallen on hard times, that's all.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_012: Haven't you heard about the daughter of the Dyan-\nsupporting noble who signed up? Well, that's me.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_013: Prince Dyan? The man who launched a failed coup,\nresulting in disgrace for his supporters?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_014: That's the one. So now do you get why I act like this?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_015: No. If you know better, then your behavior is even\nmore outrageous.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_016: No matter your circumstances, you should comport\nyourself nobly and exercise self-discipline.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_017: Ugh. I knew you wouldn't get it.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_018: I'll just say this. No one on Queen Theodora's side\nwill ever trust anyone from Dyan's faction.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_019: So take the hint and stay away. You don't want any\nguilt by association.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_020: Also out of the question. I can't stand by silently\nwhen a comrade in arms is embarrassing herself.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_021: Oh, so you're gonna be my babysitter? Is this lecture\npart of that duty, then?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_022: Er—no. I mean, yes, I do intend to keep an eye on\nyou here and there, but...
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_023: I believe the hand of fate is at work in us coming\ntogether as allies.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_024: Now that we both serve Her Majesty, I want to\nencourage each other and work together!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_025: Being annoying comes so naturally to you, huh?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_026: Don't mock me! This scornful attitude won't get\nyou anywhere.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_027: If the troops think you guilty by association, then you\nshould prove them wrong with your actions.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_028: Wow, it sounds so easy when you put it like that.\nYou don't know what you're talking about, rich boy.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_029: Like you're one to talk! You were born into privilege\nyourself, weren't you?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_030: You don't get me because you've never lost anything.\nJust go away.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_C_031: Lilian! Ugh. I'll have to try again some other time.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_001: Mrrgrr...
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_002: You know, I'm not sure it counts as surveillance\nwhen you're that obvious about it.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_003: So you noticed. I'm not very practiced at these\nunderhanded maneuvers.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_004: What's so underhanded about tailing someone?\nSpoken like a true rich boy.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_005: Quit teasing me! I like my fights open and\naboveboard, that's all.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_006: When I make a name for myself, it will be without\nrelying on my status as the chancellor's nephew.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_007: If you want. But your status is an asset. It's silly not\nto use it.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_008: Abusing one's station to get ahead is underhanded.\nI would never—
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_009: Yeah, yeah, you'll do it all on your own without any\nhelp from anyone. Spare me.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_010: That's pure pride, is what that is. And you'll regret it\nif it ends up holding you back.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_011: Then what about you? Your attitude around Her\nMajesty is as foul as ever!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_012: Is it not holding you back as a soldier to defy your\nliege? You don't have a shred of loyalty!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_013: Loyalty? Oh, I'd say my attitude is plenty reasonable.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_014: My estate and my life with my family were taken\nfrom me because my father sided with Dyan.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_015: That's why I don't like Queen Theodora. I signed up\nwith her for my reasons, not hers.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_016: Do you have any idea how it feels to bend the knee\nto the woman who ruined your life?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_017: I'm sorry. I never considered how difficult your\nposition must be.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_018: Spare me the melodrama. Just tell me—what's in this\nfor you?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_019: Why do you want to make a name for yourself\nso bad? What is "loyalty" to you?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_020: As a proud soldier of Saramis in service to Her\nMajesty—
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_021: We're all soldiers here, doofus. I want to know what\nYOU think.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_022: Well...you see, as the son of my esteemed father...
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_023: Ugh. More rich-boy talk, huh? I'm out.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_024: Wait, Lilian! You're right that I don't have an answer\nfor you just yet.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_025: But I will find one! So let's pick up again here\nwhen I do.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_026: So melodramatic. Fine, I'll be waiting. But I'm not\ngetting my hopes up.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_027: I admire Lilian. She's prepared to sacrifice for her\ngoals, no matter the circumstances. While I...
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_B_028: Does that make my loyalty a sham? What is loyalty?\nAnd what is it that drives me?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_001: Lilian! I heard that you finally warmed toward\nHer Majesty.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_002: You could say that. The queen and me are cool now.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_003: "Cool"? You make yourself sound like Her Majesty's\nbest friend. This is another form of disrespect.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_004: That aside, have you truly forgiven Her Majesty?\nShe did seize your estate.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_005: Well, as a certain someone once said, a scornful\nattitude won't get me anywhere.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_006: Touché. Those words are a bit embarrassing in\nhindsight.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_007: Hey, they were what finally convinced me that\nQueen Theodora is a great leader.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_008: My duties have also shown me that she is a queen\nworthy of my loyalty.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_009: Lilian, I believe I am now ready to answer the\nquestion you posed before.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_010: My overeagerness to distinguish myself is not loyalty.\nIt is a virtue unrelated to glory.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_011: You know what, Lysander? I like the fire in your\neyes you've got going lately.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_012: Er...thank you. I, um, could say the same of you.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_013: Oh yeah? Heh. That means I've grown as a\nperson, right?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_014: Thinking back, I believe we got off on the wrong\nfoot. Largely due to my immaturity.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_015: But starting now, I believe we can better work hand\nin hand to serve Her Majesty.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_016: Just take it easy, OK? I'm not as zealous as you\nabout this stuff.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_017: Heh. Still insolent, but it takes on a different cast\nthese days.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_018: Probably because I learned you have a heart inside.\nYou asked me the hard questions I needed to hear.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_019: Eh. Part of that was just spite. It's not like I cared\nthen about an answer.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_020: I was so happy you saw me for myself, rather than\nKleitos's son or the chancellor's nephew.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_021: Hm! Just what I expect to hear from an incorrigible\nflirt like you.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_022: A flirt? Me?! What do you mean?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_023: I know how you play the field. Those corny lines\nare like catnip to your type.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_024: W-well, I won't say I've NEVER flirted with a\nwoman, but...it never goes anywhere serious!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_025: I decided early on that I wouldn't marry until I had\nsurpassed my father.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_026: That's kinda cool. My parents mean a lot to me too,\nso I get it.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_027: Right. So it probably will be some time until I can\nadmit my feelings for you.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_028: Wait, back up. "Feelings"? Like, FEELINGS feelings?
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_029: But enough of that! Let us work hard together to\nbecome exemplary retainers.
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_030: It's almost time for our daily patrol. Don't fall behind!
MID_SE_Lil_Lys_A_031: Hey! Get back here, Lysander! My heart's already\nracing before this turns into a race!